#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:UnanchoredDiagnosticShape (Rule D1): a
# math:ModelDiagnostic anchored to BOTH what it evaluates and how — it names the
# math:FittedModel it checks through math:diagnosticFor (satisfying the sh:minCount 1
# fitted-model arm) and the method it applies through math:diagnosticMethod (satisfying
# the sh:minCount 1 method arm). The fitted model itself is well-formed — bound to its
# data through math:fittedToData and specified through math:modelFormula — so
# math:UnfittedModel stays silent. A diagnostic that names both its fit and its method is
# well-formed and MUST raise NO failure class.
# Positive counterpart of counter-examples/diagnostic-unanchored.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecDiagnosticAnchored).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

# The evaluation: a diagnostic naming its fit AND its method.
ex:residualDiagnostic a math:ModelDiagnostic ;
    math:diagnosticFor ex:trialFit ;
    math:diagnosticMethod ex:residualAnalysis .

ex:residualAnalysis a math:MathematicalObject .   # the diagnostic method, a first-class object

# The fit it evaluates: a well-formed math:FittedModel (data + specification).
ex:trialFit a math:FittedModel ;
    math:fittedToData ex:trialData ;
    math:modelFormula ex:trialFormula .

ex:trialData a math:DatasetMatrix .
ex:trialFormula a math:ModelFormula .
